[0.009, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m- Both repos' feature-base are pushed and clean:\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - Jettison 82848fe \"Format: a blank line above a comment that follows code\".\u001b[39m                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - Manifest 4558791 \"Format: the engine's declaration and comment spacing applied\".\u001b[39m                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - Manifest pins Jettison 7a2d936. The commit after it is blank lines only, so no re-pin is needed.\u001b[39m                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m- All lanes are parked, detached at feature-base: jettison.lane-b/c, manifest.lane-b/c.\u001b[39m                               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m- Recently done:\u001b[39m                                                                                                      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - J01 adopted in Manifest: sealed connections, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mmanifest-token key\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--serve --key\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m, and the client pins the key from \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mserve\u001b[9Gs.yaml.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - Manifest's suites fixed for the tote rescale (80d1df7).\u001b[39m                                                           \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m  - The comment-spacing rule is in scripts/space-declarations.py and the coding standards. It applies to Manifest \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwith \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--root\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m. No formatting change ever reaches inside a string or other literal.\u001b[39m                                      \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mOpen question, a balance one, not urgent: the scenarios' stock is counted in totes, and a tote now holds fewer units,\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mso foods sell out at Forge. The development fixture buys soap instead of rice to get around it. Rescaling the stocks\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mchanges behaviour that the trade and company suites check.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mNext: read docs/roadmap.md and ../manifest/docs/delivery-order.md for the next task. Run scripts/lanes.sh to pick a \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mlane. Tell me the model and effort you recommend before you start. Follow AGENTS.md, the coding standards and memory:\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mcommit only when I ask, stage files by name, one heavy gate at a time, and push with the sandbox disabled.\u001b[39m            \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[3GOrchestrat\u001b[38;2;235;159;127ming\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;255;193;7m⏵⏵ auto mode on\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
