[0.083, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H  The roadmap also says Manifest's later work waits until you've played the first loop for a day or two.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mWhat I propose, for you to settle:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  1. \u001b[1mSplit W22.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     - \u001b[1mW22a:\u001b[22m the drive record, the radius in \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCruiseDrive\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mClearOf\u001b[39m, deuterium pellets as a trade good, and one medium\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B       freighter of about 3,000 t on the hauler drive that docks at the existing destroyer pad.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     - \u001b[1mW22b:\u001b[22m the pulse carrier with its dry dock, the licence, and the override's fine and harm.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  2. \u001b[1mHand the freighter over in a scenario's starting fleet.\u001b[22m Buying it stays with L48.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  3. \u001b[1mThe numbers in D-108 were an agent's proposal.\u001b[22m Do you accept them as written (3% exhaust, 0.3 g sustained, 1,000 km\r\u001b[1B     radius)?\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mIf you'd rather not wait on those answers:\u001b[22m J02, the top of Jettison's backlog in Tier 1, is the alternative. It's the\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  rule for whose authority a script's command carries under networked play, which needs to be settled before players\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  rely on it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mModel and effort:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G- \u001b[1mW22a: Opus 5.5, high effort.\u001b[22m It changes\u001b[45Gsaved ship state, the cru\u001b[71Gse, the policy's estimates\u001b[98Gand\u001b[102Gthe\u001b[106Gcompany's\r\u001b[1B    provisioning. A cheaper model risks a sloppy save format and cruise logic that later work is built\u001b[104Gon.\r\u001b[1B  - \u001b[1mJ02: Opus 5.5, high effort.\u001b[33G\u001b[22mIt's\u001b[38Gan\u001b[41Gauthority\u001b[51Grule\u001b[56Gthat\u001b[61Gends\u001b[66Gup\u001b[69Gin\u001b[72Gever